---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';

const entry = {
  "id": "harvard_vi4_545",
  "series": "Band VI 4 (1677 - 1690)",
  "seq": 545,
  "text": " [[2514.27]] <b>430₁.  Auszug Mai 1677 AUSZUG </p>\n<p> [[2515.1]] Maji 1677 </p>\n<p> [[2515.2]] P. Fridericus Spee e Soc. Jesu pauca sed praeclara ingenii sui monumenta reliquit.\n[[2515.3]] Scripsit <i>Cautionem Criminalem de Processu contra Sagas</i>, cui nomen suum praefigere\n[[2515.4]] ausus non est; ubi candide admodum ostendit quam stulta ac malitiose multa in hoc\n[[2515.5]] negotio gerantur. Sed divinus mihi plane visus est libellus ejus lingua Germanica scriptus,\n[[2515.6]] cui titulus est: <i>Gülden-tugend-Kleinod</i>, quem vellem in omnium Christianorum esse\n[[2515.7]] manibus. Multi habentur autores mysticae theologiae, sed an unquam quisquam tanta\n[[2515.8]] solidae pietatis specimina scripto dederit, nescio. Florida hic eloquentia et coeleste\n[[2515.9]] quiddam spirans, sententiae pulcherrimae, expressiones lucidae et naturales, inventiones\n[[2515.10]] ingeniosae et jucundae. Quod si delicatas poëseos Germanicae leges scivisset, quae tum\n[[2515.11]] primum natae sunt, et quidem inter Protestantes, ad Catholicos autem sero ac ne nunc\n[[2515.12]] quidem plane pervenere; posset libellus autoris nostri quem vocat <i>Truz-Nachtigall</i>, inter\n[[2515.13]] linguae nostrae ornamenta censeri. Sed ut ad solida revertar, mirifice affectus sum,\n[[2515.14]] quoties ea legi quae de natura et efficacia amoris Dei super omnia disseruit. Nescio enim\n[[2515.15]] an quisquam unquam autorum qui in populi usum scripsere rem tantam uno nostro autore\n[[2515.16]] excepto pro dignitate attigerit. Ostendit enim in quo vera consistat natura contritionis et\n[[2515.17]] Amoris Deo debiti, idque familiari sermone et ad commovendos homines apto. Viam\n[[2515.18]] quin etiam subindicat, per quam unusquisque ad contritionem pervenire possit, ne sibi\n[[2515.19]] imaginentur homines veram contritionem et actum amoris Dei super omnia esse rem ad\n[[2515.20]] quam post omnem conatum adhibitum non semper liceat pervenire. Quin imo clare\n[[2515.21]] edisserit, qui hunc amorem non habeat eum esse in statu mortalis peccati, ut scilicet tacite\n[[2515.22]] innueret (: nam totidem verbis efferre credo ausus non est :), attritionem solam etiam cum\n[[2515.23]] poenitentiae sacramento non sufficere ad remissionem peccati et justificationem: contra\n[[2515.24]] vulgarem Scholasticorum opinionem, nuper in Gallia recte impugnatam. Ut vero vis\n[[2515.25]] divini amoris magis elucesceret, haec sane praeclara habet: Si quis omnibus omnium\n[[2516.1]] peccatis oneratus esset, si omnes damnatorum atque daemonum in eum nequitiae confluxissent;\n[[2516.2]] jamque veniret super eum spiritus domini, et amorem Dei super omnia accenderet,\n[[2516.3]] dubium nullum est, quin ab illo ipso momento omnia ei peccata remitterentur,\n[[2516.4]] etiam antequam ea ulli sacerdoti fuisset confessus. Autores citat Gabrielem, Vegam,\n[[2516.5]] Navarrum. Addit hoc amplius, si ne cogitaret quidem de peccatis suis, atque ita neque\n[[2516.6]] veniam peteret, neque de commissis doleret tamen remitterentur. Quoniam vera poenitentia\n[[2516.7]] in actu supremi amoris potentia continetur. </p>\n<p> [[2516.8]] Hoc est verum theologiae arcanae mysterium, quod nescio an quisquam (in Germania\n[[2516.9]] certe) praeter P. Spee populo propalare ausus sit, cum tamen nihil sit utilius, nihil\n[[2516.10]] efficacius, nihil necessarium magis. </p>\n<p> [[2516.11]] Ait quidem etiam fidem et spem, esse ad salutem necessarias, sed satis ostendit eam\n[[2516.12]] se intelligere fidem, sine qua ea quam requirit Caritas amorque Dei subsistere non potest.\n[[2516.13]] Nimirum ait necesse esse, ut credat aliquis et esse Deum, et summe potentem, sapientem,\n[[2516.14]] bonum, perfectum, amore summo dignum esse. Alia omnia speciatim ne attingit quidem:\n[[2516.15]] ut innueret in his totam fidei salutiferae vim contineri. Equidem addit, peccata postea\n[[2516.16]] confitenda esse sacerdoti, quando primum id fieri potest, obedientiae causa: Item credenda\n[[2516.17]] esse quaecunque proponit Ecclesia Catholica. Sed hoc intelligendum est haud\n[[2516.18]] dubie de homine per quem non stat, quo minus id facere possit. Idque praeclare innuit\n[[2516.19]] autor noster, cum ait amorem Dei super omnia sine vera fide esse non posse. Cum\n[[2516.20]] manifestum sit posse aliquem amare Deum animitus velut summum Bonum, eique\n[[2516.21]] quantum ejus mens assequi potest, pronissima voluntate obsequi, etiamsi ne verbulum\n[[2516.22]] quidem audierit de Ecclesiae dogmatis, modo pertinacia et inobedientia absit, quae sane\n[[2516.23]] cum caritate stare non potest. </p>\n",
  "number": "430₁.",
  "title": "Auszug Mai 1677",
  "date": null
};
---

<Layout title={`${entry.title || entry.id} - Leibniz Writings`}>
  <article data-pagefind-body>
    <header class="entry-header">
      <h1 data-pagefind-meta="title">{entry.title || entry.id}</h1>

      <div class="entry-meta">
        {entry.date && (
          <div class="meta-item">
            <strong>Date:</strong>
            <span data-pagefind-meta="date">{entry.date}</span>
          </div>
        )}

        <div class="meta-item">
          <strong>Series:</strong>
          <span data-pagefind-meta="series">{entry.series}</span>
        </div>

        {entry.number && (
          <div class="meta-item">
            <strong>Number:</strong>
            <span data-pagefind-meta="number">{entry.number}</span>
          </div>
        )}

        <div class="meta-item">
          <strong>Sequence:</strong>
          <span>{entry.seq}</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </header>

    <!-- View Toggle -->
    <div class="view-controls">
      <button id="translation-view-btn" class="view-btn active">Translation View</button>
      <button id="scholarly-view-btn" class="view-btn">Scholarly View</button>
    </div>

    <div class="entry-content" data-pagefind-meta="excerpt:430₁. Auszug Mai 1677 AUSZUG Maji 1677 P. Fridericus Spee e Soc. Jesu pauca sed praeclara ingenii sui monumenta reliquit. Scripsit Cautionem Criminalem de Processu contra Sagas, cui nomen suum praefigere ausus non est; ubi candide admodum ostendit quam stulta ac malitiose multa in hoc negotio gerant...">

      <!-- Translation-friendly continuous text -->
      <div id="translation-view" class="text-view active">
        <div class="translation-notice">
          <p><strong>📖 Translation View:</strong> Continuous text optimized for browser translation tools.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="continuous-text" translate="yes" lang="unknown" id="continuous-text">
          <!-- Will be populated by JavaScript -->
        </div>
        <div class="line-numbers-reference" id="line-numbers-ref">
          <!-- Will be populated by JavaScript -->
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Detailed scholarly view with line numbers -->
      <div id="scholarly-view" class="text-view">
        <div class="scholarly-notice">
          <p><strong>📚 Scholarly View:</strong> Original text with line number annotations preserved.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="annotated-text" id="annotated-text">
          {entry.text.split('\n').map(paragraph =>
            paragraph.trim() && <p set:html={paragraph} />
          )}
        </div>
      </div>

    </div>
  </article>

  <nav class="entry-navigation">
    <a href="/" class="back-link">← Back to Search</a>
  </nav>
</Layout>

<style>
  .entry-header {
    margin-bottom: 30px;
    padding-bottom: 20px;
    border-bottom: 2px solid var(--border);
  }

  .entry-header h1 {
    color: var(--primary);
    font-size: 2rem;
    margin-bottom: 20px;
    line-height: 1.3;
  }

  .entry-meta {
    display: grid;
    gap: 8px;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
  }

  .meta-item {
    display: flex;
    align-items: flex-start;
    gap: 8px;
  }

  .meta-item strong {
    color: var(--text);
    min-width: 80px;
  }

  .meta-item span {
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    flex: 1;
  }

  .entry-content {
    margin-bottom: 40px;
  }

  .text-content {
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 30px;
    line-height: 1.7;
  }

  .text-content :global(p) {
    margin-bottom: 16px;
  }

  .text-content :global(p:last-child) {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  .text-content :global(b) {
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--primary);
  }

  .entry-navigation {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
    padding-top: 20px;
  }

  .back-link {
    color: var(--primary);
    text-decoration: none;
    font-weight: 500;
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 8px;
    transition: color 0.2s;
  }

  .back-link:hover {
    color: var(--primary-dark);
    text-decoration: underline;
  }

  /* View Toggle Controls */
  .view-controls {
    display: flex;
    gap: 8px;
    margin-bottom: 20px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
    padding-bottom: 20px;
  }

  .view-btn {
    background: transparent;
    border: 2px solid var(--border);
    padding: 8px 16px;
    border-radius: 6px;
    cursor: pointer;
    font-size: 14px;
    font-weight: 500;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    transition: all 0.2s;
  }

  .view-btn:hover {
    border-color: var(--primary);
    color: var(--primary);
  }

  .view-btn.active {
    background: var(--primary);
    border-color: var(--primary);
    color: white;
  }

  /* Text Views */
  .text-view {
    display: none;
  }

  .text-view.active {
    display: block;
  }

  /* Translation View */
  .translation-notice, .scholarly-notice {
    background: var(--background);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 6px;
    padding: 12px;
    margin-bottom: 20px;
    font-size: 14px;
  }

  .continuous-text {
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 2px solid var(--primary);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 25px;
    line-height: 1.8;
    font-size: 16px;
    color: var(--text);
    margin-bottom: 15px;
  }

  .line-numbers-reference {
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    font-size: 13px;
    padding: 10px;
    background: var(--background);
    border-radius: 4px;
  }

  /* Scholarly View */
  .annotated-text {
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 20px;
  }

  .text-line {
    display: flex;
    align-items: flex-start;
    margin-bottom: 8px;
    gap: 12px;
  }

  .line-refs {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 4px;
    min-width: 80px;
    flex-shrink: 0;
  }

  .line-num {
    background: var(--primary);
    color: white;
    padding: 2px 6px;
    border-radius: 4px;
    font-size: 11px;
    font-weight: 600;
    font-family: monospace;
  }

  .line-content {
    flex: 1;
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  .line-content :global(b) {
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--primary);
  }

  .line-content :global(i) {
    font-style: italic;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
  }

  @media (min-width: 768px) {
    .entry-meta {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
    }
  }

  @media (max-width: 768px) {
    .view-controls {
      flex-direction: column;
    }

    .text-line {
      flex-direction: column;
      gap: 6px;
    }

    .line-refs {
      min-width: auto;
    }
  }
</style>

<script>
  // Process text for translation view
  function processTextForTranslation(text) {
    if (!text) return { translationText: '', lineNumbers: [] };

    const lines = text.split('\n');
    let translationText = '';
    const lineNumbers = [];

    lines.forEach(line => {
      const trimmedLine = line.trim();
      if (!trimmedLine) return;

      // Extract line numbers
      const lineNumberMatch = trimmedLine.match(/\[\[(\d+\.\d+)\]\]/g);
      const extractedNumbers = lineNumberMatch ?
        lineNumberMatch.map(m => m.replace(/\[|\]/g, '')) : [];

      // Remove line number markers and HTML tags for continuous text
      let contentOnly = trimmedLine
        .replace(/\[\[\d+\.\d+\]\]/g, '')
        .replace(/<\/?[^>]+(>|$)/g, '')
        .replace(/\s+/g, ' ')
        .trim();

      if (contentOnly) {
        if (translationText) translationText += ' ';
        translationText += contentOnly;
        lineNumbers.push(...extractedNumbers);
      }
    });

    return {
      translationText: translationText.trim(),
      lineNumbers: lineNumbers
    };
  }

  // View switching and text processing
  document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', () => {
    const translationBtn = document.getElementById('translation-view-btn');
    const scholarlyBtn = document.getElementById('scholarly-view-btn');
    const translationView = document.getElementById('translation-view');
    const scholarlyView = document.getElementById('scholarly-view');
    const continuousTextDiv = document.getElementById('continuous-text');
    const lineNumbersRef = document.getElementById('line-numbers-ref');

    // Process the text for translation view
    if (continuousTextDiv && lineNumbersRef && entry && entry.text) {
      const processed = processTextForTranslation(entry.text);
      continuousTextDiv.textContent = processed.translationText;

      if (processed.lineNumbers.length > 0) {
        lineNumbersRef.innerHTML = `<small><strong>Line numbers:</strong> ${processed.lineNumbers.join(', ')}</small>`;
      }
    }

    // View switching functionality
    if (translationBtn && scholarlyBtn && translationView && scholarlyView) {
      translationBtn.addEventListener('click', () => {
        translationBtn.classList.add('active');
        scholarlyBtn.classList.remove('active');
        translationView.classList.add('active');
        scholarlyView.classList.remove('active');
      });

      scholarlyBtn.addEventListener('click', () => {
        scholarlyBtn.classList.add('active');
        translationBtn.classList.remove('active');
        scholarlyView.classList.add('active');
        translationView.classList.remove('active');
      });
    }
  });
</script>